      "side": 1,
      "message": "This looks hard to understand ; could you not just have the caller call invokeEnterMethods if invokeExitMethods didn\u0027t fail ?\n\nCase in point : if any of the exit methods fail, your current code will try to enter the stack anyway without exiting. Example :\n\n    SyncMachine\n    └ A\n      └ B\n        └ C\n    └ D\n      └ E\n\nSuppose you are in C and try to transition to E. Desired sequence :\n• C.exit\n• B.exit\n• A.exit\n• D.enter\n• E.enter\n\nNow suppose B.exit returns FAILURE, your code will not execute A.exit but it will still execute D.enter (and if D.enter succeeds, E.enter). I think this is unexpected.",
